    {
      "id": "generated-union-macro",
      "kind": "static",
      "features": [
        "generated-noneditable"
      ],
      "mainFileId": "main",
      "documents": [
        {
          "fileId": "main",
          "path": "main.tex",
          "content": "\\newcommand{\\join}[2]{#1\\mathbin{\\cup}#2}\nSuppose \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are subsets of a fixed universe \\(U\\). We claim that\nthe least subset of \\(U\\) containing each of them is their union. Indeed,\nfor every \\(x\\in U\\),\n\\[\n  x\\in\\join{A}{B}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad (x\\in A)\\lor(x\\in B).\n\\]\nConsequently any set \\(C\\subseteq U\\) that contains both \\(A\\) and \\(B\\)\nalso contains \\(\\join{A}{B}\\). This proves the claim.\n"
        }
